{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074887-controlling-paradox-scelesti","id":1074887,"title":"Controlling Paradox (Scelesti)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-07T15:48:52-07:00","id":1074887,"title":"Controlling Paradox (Scelesti)","content":"So, being new to the 2nd edition of Mage, explain this to me like I'm five: how do Mages invite Paradox into their spells, thus corrupting them and making them more powerful? How is this addicting? Provided examples would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Secondly, how does swearing yourself to an Abyssal Watchtower or gaining a Scelesti Legacy work in this new edition? What benefits does it grant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There was a signature here. It's gone now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8730-pandorym","name":"Pandorym","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8730_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T19:12:29-07:00","id":1074951,"title":"","content":"Joining a Ziggurat would be much the same as in Tome of the Mysteries, and joining a Scelesti Legacy isn't really any different than joining a normal one.<br /> <br /> Not sure enough on the rest to really comment meaningfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T19:18:53-07:00","id":1074954,"title":"","content":"Without speaking of that which has not been written, it looks like 'inviting Paradox' into a spell is the thing in the brief Scelesti systems section. They don't contest the Paradox roll for casting, and instead roll Gnosis, with each success allowing them to control one Reach applied by the Paradox roll. It suggests your storyteller crafts further details, though I'd wager a player and storyteller could work them out together just fine, for further ways to control the Paradox pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T16:11:48-07:00","id":1076693,"title":"","content":"I think it would basically be that as a Mage, every time you cast a Spell you can feel the Abyss at the edges trying to worm its way in and cause Paradox. Normally a Mage uses their will to force that not to happen (it's automatic, since forming an Imago means you have to picture your intended results perfectly you fight changes it to it naturally). Instead a Mage could try to harness that incoming Abyssal energy and let it change their spell in just the way they want (or so they think, HUBRIS!).<br /> <br /> Like when they cast and feel a push of Paradox try to make the spell larger and more destructive, rather than fighting it, they let that bit of Paradox in so the spell gets bigger than they could have done alone (applying the Paradox Reach to move to Advanced Scale for example).<br /> <br /> On the surface it is addicting the same way any power/magic is. You get to control more than you could and after you succeed once, it's tempting to try again, maybe a bit further this time, and then even more the next time, and so on. The Adept is suddenly casting with the Reach of a Master, that sounds addicting in its own right.<br /> <br /> You can add in a more Abyssal specific addictiveness too, maybe there is a bit of surge of feeling or a voice in the back of your head, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Added a bit about addiction. 04-11-2017, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T16:39:47-07:00","id":1076703,"title":"","content":"So apparently this thread was double posted here (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...radox-scelesti</a>).<br /> <br /> My response may have fallen on deaf ears... Also in the other thread Dave went into way more detail and shared so much goodness.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Mod could merge them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack